# Review: Feeds

The spec says nothing in it is built, and the code agrees: there are no branches in the feed layer.
What exists is the base the spec describes under "What exists". A `Feed` is an append log of ECHO
objects; `Obj.update` re-appends a whole object by id; `FeedProtocol.Block` carries the fields and the
per-space, per-namespace `position` the spec names; soft fork (`Feed.PARENT_KEY`, `Feed.history`)
gives per-item lineage inside one feed. Every branch requirement (removal, per-branch index, heads,
partial sync, per-branch retention) is missing, and indexing, retention and sync are all per feed.
The trajectory design (#13782) and the `Thread` 0.3.0 comment feeds (#14206) are not on `main`, so
`Trajectory.Event` and `threadOpen` have no code in this checkout.

Of 20 items: 2 done, 0 untested, 5 partial, 1 diverged, 12 missing. Three findings matter most:

- **Rewind is its own mechanism.** [F-1.5] asks for rewind to be a branch plus a removal; the code
  rewinds through `Feed.rewindFrom` and per-item `PARENT_KEY` lineage, which `Feed.history` resolves
  at read time.
- **Everything is per feed.** `Feed.IndexingOptions`, `Feed.RetentionOptions`, `Feed.sync` and
  `Scope.feed` take a feed and nothing finer, so [F-2.1], [F-2.3] and [F-4.4] have no hook to build on.
- **Local order is on its way out.** `Block.insertionId` is the only local order, and it carries a
  `TODO(dmaretskyi): Remove. Use cursors.`; the local cursor API #13782 adds is not on `main`.

